## Objective
- Act as an autonomous bug-bounty agent per `skills/AGENT.md`: find valid, reproducible, high-impact vulnerabilities on the authorized URLs in `data/targets.txt`, then report them under `result/`.

## Important Details
- Repo root: `/home/runner/work/aaii-aautomattionn/aaii-aautomattionn`.
- Authorized scope (URL-list, host `console.byteplus.com`): `/waf/overview`, `/finance`, `/user`, `/beian`, `/message`, `/workorder/list/`; sub-routes and same-origin JS/APIs of these routes only.
- Rules: no scope expansion; record out-of-scope items in `result/out-of-scope.txt`; evidence only from execution/runtime observation; never claim confirmed without proof; client-side bugs first per sub-route, then server-side.
- Test accounts (public/disposable, from `creds/test-account.txt`; login `https://console.byteplus.com/auth/login/`):
  - A: `adoringjepsen1@fearlessmails.com` / `Acd3423@#345566` — Account ID `3000823185`, name `test-user-123`.
  - B: `testt456` / `Acd3423@#345` — Account ID `3001021825`.
- Environment: headless Chrome `156.0.8078.73`, DevTools at `http://127.0.0.1:9222`; node v22.23.4, python 3.14.4, curl 8.18.0.
- Tooling quirks: `rg` not installed; Grep tool fails on minified JS (`Ripgrep JSON record exceeded 65536 bytes`) — use `python3` regex scripts instead.
- A's CSRF token: `b875734d2843a16818ed6674ff180bbe`; `csrfToken` cookie is readable via `document.cookie`. Browser `fetch` with `credentials:'include'` + `x-csrf-token` works for same-origin API testing.
- Earlier runs were watchdog-terminated; current run decision `preserved` (target hash `10b1d70394a4c788e878fcaed6a267d875fe2aa39485f57f4891ff81499783ca` unchanged). Session started `2026-10-29T10:16:12Z`; testing began ~`10:43Z`.

## Work State
### Completed
- Read `skills/AGENT.md`, `skills/client-side-skill.md`, `skills/server-side-skill.md`, `data/targets.txt`, `creds/`, existing `result/` state.
- Created output scaffolding: `result/testing-inventory.json`, `result/inventory/{routes,javascript,endpoints,sinks,listeners}.md`, `result/logs/client-side.log`; appended continuation note to `result/logs/session.md`.
- Logged in as account A; session valid on `https://console.byteplus.com/home`.
- Route `/waf/overview`: redirects to `https://console.byteplus.com/iam/service/attach_role/?ServiceName=waf`; marked **unresolved** (test account lacks WAF service role; did not perform the state-changing authorization).
- Route `/finance`: redirects to `/finance/overview`, accessible, no bills ($0.00). `/finance/bill` → `/finance/bill/detail`, no rows. Sub-routes extracted from JS `main.def4a3cd.js` / `2388.6a141900.js`: `overview, bill, bill/detail, cost-analyse, invoice-manage, payment-methods, coupon, order, contract, transactions, budget-detail, budget-edit, resource-package, saving-plan, split-bill, transfer/:Status/:AccountID/:TransferApplicationNo, voucher/:PickupVoucherID, sign-quote/:contractNo, mail-detail/:contractNo, details/:Type/:AccountID/:TransferApplicationNo, detail/:OrderID`, etc.
- Route `/user`: redirects to `/user/basics/`; sub-routes `/user/basics/`, `/user/security/`, `/user/authentication/`, `/user/paymentMethod`; menu = Basic information / Real name verification / Payment method / Security settings. `/user/security/` loaded and captured.
- Route `/message`: redirects to `/message/innermsg`; detail URL `https://console.byteplus.com/message/innermsg/detail?InnermsgId=34890166`. Observed iframe `id="external-frame"` with `srcdoc` length 4868 and `sandbox=null` — potential stored-XSS sink if message content is attacker-influenced (unproven).
- Logged in as account B in isolated context (`isolatedContext=accountB`, page 2) to obtain its Account ID for cross-account tests.
- IDOR probe result: `AccountID` query param is ignored server-side — `GetCountryAreaCfgByAccountID` and `QueryCreditProtocolDetail` returned A's account (`3000823185`) even when `AccountID=3001021825`; protected (negative result).
- Downloaded route JS for offline analysis: `/tmp/finance` (`main.def4a3cd.js` sha256 `fa0268ff...`, `2388.6a141900.js` sha256 `fdf5440a...`, `lib-router.344a8bb5.js`), `/tmp/user` (`main.4ec0f485.js` sha256 `61fcdc0d...`, `1834.03734ebf.js`, `builder-runtime.b5328f1b.js`), `/tmp/msg` (`main.5bc4931c.js` sha256 `5c953209...`, `337.8f0884ae.js` sha256 `4bf3f20b...`, `builder-runtime.e7955615.js`).

### Active
- Investigating the `/message` `external-frame` `srcdoc` sink: identifying which async chunk sets `srcdoc` and whether content can be attacker-controlled (e.g., support-ticket title/body, account display name) and delivered cross-user.
- Message-detail scripts still to fetch: `.../bp-vconsole-message/static/js/1.0.0.435/async/message_innermsg.f9a63668.js`, `async/709.f00821bc.js`, `async/853.6ebc1a89.js`, `async/264.e6289711.js`, `async/286.368ceaf1.js`, `async/976.32ececa6.js`, `async/426.84469f54.js`.

### Blocked
- `/waf/overview` blocked by missing WAF service role (cross-service authorization page); not expanding via state change.
- Grep tool unusable on minified bundles (record-size error); `rg` missing.
- No bill/invoice/order data on test account A, limiting finance server-side object tests.

