## Objective
- Act as an autonomous bug-bounty agent per `skills/AGENT.md`: find valid, reproducible, high-impact vulnerabilities on the authorized URLs in `data/targets.txt`, then report them under `result/`.

## Important Details
- Repo root: `/home/runner/work/aaii-aautomattionn/aaii-aautomattionn`.
- Authorized scope (URL-list, host `console.byteplus.com`): `/waf/overview`, `/finance`, `/user`, `/beian`, `/message`, `/workorder/list/`; only these routes and their sub-routes + same-origin JS/APIs.
- Rules: no scope expansion; out-of-scope items to `result/out-of-scope.txt`; evidence only from execution/runtime observation; never claim confirmed without runtime proof; append only high-impact confirmed findings to `result/confirmed-vuln.txt` (XSS with real JS execution, CSTI, IDOR, BAC, or open redirect allowing `javascript:`).
- Test accounts: A `adoringjepsen1@fearlessmails.com`/`Acd3423@#345566` (account 3000823185); B `testt456`/`Acd3423@#345` (account 3001021825). Credentials are intentionally public/disposable.
- Chrome DevTools MCP at `http://127.0.0.1:9222` (Chrome/156.0.8078.73). Watchdog kills after ~2 min without tool output — keep tool calls frequent.
- Prior run history preserved only in `result/logs/opencode.log` (583KB); `/tmp` from prior runs is gone.
- Prior verified negatives: ticket stored XSS payloads sanitized server-side (format-independent, confirmed on write); `UpdateTicket` extra fields ignored; billing endpoints scoped by session; message detail uses DOMPurify 2.5.9 + server sanitizer; user app React-escaped; SDK postMessage listeners strict.
- `vulnebleti/Fuzz/control-character-techniques.md` explicitly hints at `console.byteplus.com/auth/login/?redirectURI=` open redirect — this matched the confirmed finding.
- `/waf/overview` redirects to IAM cross-service authorization page (test account lacks WAF service role; not authorized → unresolved).
- `/beian` previously 404.
- `/message/org/recipient` redirects to `/message/innermsg` for B; batch-add recipients disabled.
- `iframe#external-frame` on message detail has `sandbox=null` with `srcdoc` = server-generated email template ("Ticket I-... Has a New Reply"); no user-controlled HTML injection observed there.

## Work State
### Completed
- Read `skills/AGENT.md`, `skills/client-side-skill.md`, `skills/server-side-skill.md`; loaded `data/targets.txt`, `creds/`, `result/scope.md`, inventories, prior logs.
- Confirmed **VULN-20261029-001 — Open redirect via auth `redirectURI` tab bypass**:
  - Payload `/%09/evil.com/` (decodes `/	/evil.com/`).
  - Already-authenticated victim visiting `https://console.byteplus.com/auth/login/?redirectURI=%2F%09%2Fevil.com%2F` auto-navigates to `https://evil.com/` (no prompt).
  - Fresh login flow: `?redirectURI=%2F%09%2Fexample.com%2F` → after login lands on `https://example.com/`; network `POST /api/passport/login/mixtureLogin` with `referer` containing payload, then `GET https://example.com/`.
  - Absolute URLs, `//host`, and `/\host` rejected (land on `/home`); tab bypasses. `javascript:` did NOT execute (`chrome-error://chromewebdata/` 403); excluded from `confirmed-vuln.txt` per rule 9, noted in report.
- Wrote finding artifacts: `result/findings/VULN-20261029-001/report.md`, `evidence/observation.md`, `payloads/redirect-uri.txt`.
- Updated `result/logs/client-side.log`, `result/inventory/routes.md`, `result/inventory/endpoints.md`, `result/testing-inventory.json`.
- Logged continuation metadata in `result/logs/session.md`.
- Recon on `/message/innermsg/detail?InnermsgId=34886574` (B-owned): inspected `external-frame` srcdoc — templated, no `<script>`/`onerror`/`javascript:`.

### Active
- Page 3 (B, isolated context `redir2`) is on `https://console.byteplus.com/finance/overview`; network captured (reqid 878–901+): `GET /api/top/account_verify/ap-southeast-1/2018-01-01/GetProfileInfo`, `GET /api/financial/const/getExpenseConfigForFE`, `GET /api/top/bill_volcano_engine/ap-singapore-1/2020-01-01/GetAccountGrayStatus`, etc. Finance page shows "Online payment is not supported in your country/region".
- Looking for B-owned finance objects (bills/orders/invoices/contracts) to attempt cross-account IDOR against A.

### Blocked
- `/waf/overview` unresolved: needs IAM cross-service role authorization (state change; not authorized).
- Account A has $0 balance/no bill rows → finance object-ID IDOR unresolved without B-owned object IDs.
- `/message` org/enterprise sub-routes unavailable to test account B (redirect to innermsg; batch add disabled).
- `javascript:` execution via `redirectURI` not achievable (verified) → open redirect remains Medium, excluded from notification bar.

## Next Move
1. Enumerate B-owned finance objects via captured finance APIs on page 3 (e.g., bill list / order list / invoice list); if IDs exist, replay as A (page 1 context via cookies or new A login) to test cross-account IDOR/BAC; record Unresolved if A inaccessible.
2. If no finance objects, test remaining `/message` setting endpoints for mass assignment (`AddMsgContact`, `UpdateMsgContactByContact`, `UpdateMessageLanguage`) with extra fields (`AccountID`, `OrganizationID`, `IsAdmin`) using test-owned data only; then finalize `result/SUMMARY.md`, `result/unresolved.md`, `result/confirmed-vuln.txt` (likely empty), session logs.

