## Work State
### Completed
- Preflight done: tools present (opencode, curl, git, node v22.23.4, python3 3.14.4, curl 8.18.0, Chrome 156.0.8078.73), Chrome DevTools MCP connected (`http://127.0.0.1:9222`).
- Wrote `result/logs/session.md` (session metadata, run_id 40856058415, reset decision) and `result/scope.md` (in/out-of-scope, URL-list target).
- Logged in; recon on `/finance`, `/user`, `/message`, `/workorder/list/` done; JS bundles downloaded and analyzed.
- Identified prior automation tickets in account: `I-2026102917080001` ("Display name rendering probe", open/Processing, used for probes), `I-2026102903090001` (MASSTEST), `I-2026102903050001` (Cross-tenant write test), `I-2026102903040001` (CSS injection test, Closed), `I-2026102903030001` (Sanitizer mapping test, Closed), `I-2026102902580001`, `I-2026102701450001`.
- Sent stored-XSS probes to `I-2026102917080001` via `POST /api/top/ticket/ap-southeast-1/2021-01-01/CreateTicketConversation` and inspected saved Content after sanitization.
- Sanitizer mapping results so far: `onerror`→removed; `<iframe srcdoc>`→removed; `<svg><a xlink:href="javascript:...">`→`<a href="" rel="...">`; plain `<a href="javascript:...">`→`href=""`; noscript mXSS→`<p>` only; math mXSS→`<table><style>` only.

### Active
- Testing server-side HTML sanitizer bypass on ticket conversation Content, aiming for stored XSS that executes in support-agent browser (validated by watching `window.__*` flags on ticket re-render).
- Last saved probe (math mXSS) result: `MBRMATH benign:<table><style>` — only `<table><style>` survived; no handler.

### Blocked
- `/waf/overview` blocked pending IAM service-role authorization (`/iam/service/attach_role/?ServiceName=waf`) — decision on whether to authorize deliberately deferred.
- Ticket API rate-limit forces slow pacing (~6–8s between calls).
- WAF 403s on some multi-vector/mXSS payloads; need single-vector isolation.

## Next Move
1. Continue isolated sanitizer-bypass probes (one vector per request, ≥6–8s apart) on ticket `I-2026102917080001`; next candidates: `<style>` tag behavior / CSS injection, `<svg><animate attributeName="href" values="javascript:...">`, `<form><button formaction="javascript:...">`, `<object>/<embed>`, `<meta http-equiv=refresh>`, entity/whitespace-encoded `javascript:` hrefs (`java&#115;cript:`, `jAvAsCrIpT:`), `data:` hrefs.
2. After each accepted probe, reload `/workorder/list/detail?id=I-2026102917080001` and check `window.__*` flags plus DOM (e.g., `querySelector('main').querySelectorAll('img')`, iframe presence) to confirm execution vs. inert storage; if confirmed, write entry to `result/confirmed-vuln.txt` per AGENT.md Section 9 and save evidence under `result/client-side/`.
3. If sanitizer holds, pivot to server-side testing: read `skills/server-side-skill.md`, then test IDOR/BAC on ticket/account APIs using both test accounts a and b, and test `redirectURI` open-redirect handling (`/user` Basics chunk module `12635`, login redirect).

